Feature: Projects API Integration

  @allure.label.suite:Projects
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: User creates project and can retrieve it
    Given the user is authenticated in a team
    When the user creates a project via API
    Then the project creation should return status 200
    And the project should have a valid ID
    When the user retrieves projects for the team
    Then the newly created project should be in the list

  @allure.label.suite:Projects
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: Project data persists across multiple API calls
    Given the user creates a project with name and description
    When the user retrieves project details
    Then the retrieved data should match the creation request
    When the user updates the project description
    And retrieves the project again
    Then the updated description should be reflected

  @allure.label.suite:Projects
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: Only team members can access team projects
    Given user A is in team X
    And user B is not in team X
    When user B attempts to access team X's projects
    Then the API should return status 403
    When user A retrieves team X's projects
    Then the API should return status 200 with project list

  @allure.label.suite:Projects
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: Project tasks are aggregated correctly
    Given a project exists
    When multiple tasks are created in the project
    And the user retrieves project details with tasks
    Then the task count should match the number of created tasks
    And all task IDs should be present in the project
